{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/68030-demon-in-a-historical-setting","id":68030,"title":"Demon in a historical setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-08T13:09:21-08:00","id":68030,"title":"Demon in a historical setting","content":"This will probably be covered in Dark Eras, but until then, I wanted to do some brainstorming about how a game like Demon with such a focus on modern technology could be run before the 20th century. How would you use Infrastructure, what would it look like, would you keep the espionage focus (it is the second oldest profession after all) or reimagine Agencies more like guilds or cults or something as the book seems to suggest?<br /> <br /> The spark for this was, i'm considering running a short mortals game as an introduction to the God-Machine/Demon for my usual players, but I want to set it in Constantinople or western Europe in the 13th century or so.The initial image I had was that the players would be dispatched by the Church to investigate a (seemingly trivial to modern eyes) heretical practice like the method of taking Communion or Mass being delivered in the common language rather than Latin, and eventually discover that the very formal, same-everywhere structure of Mass is being used as Infrastructure by the GM and the heresy is being spread by Unchained to disrupt and subvert it. I think I could take some lessons from Assassin's Creed in presenting a mostly historical setting with glimpses of hidden rooms full of highly advanced technology that the players recognize but the characters are baffled by- keeping the high technology, but changing its relationship to the PCs and emphasizing the control and power of the GM by how visibly far ahead of human technology it is.<br /> <br /> They don't all have to be medieval, but here's another idea: imagine a game where the Ring is operating out of a secluded monastery that houses/is a piece of suborned Infrastructure, researching ancient texts and relics and providing support to other Agencies, in cover as monks, garrisoned Templars and local peasants. When a papal delegation arrives to check up on the abbey and (semi-secretly) make sure they haven't become heretical away from direct Church oversight, how do the PCs avert suspicion from both mortal inquisitors and the angel that<i> has</i> to be in their party?<br /> <br /> I'm hoping we can use this thread to bounce ideas and flex our creative muscles a bit. What setpieces and ideas would you use if you were to run Demon or use elements from it in a historical setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-08-2014, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T14:19:29-08:00","id":68070,"title":"","content":"<b>tldr: I wouldn't use modern technology.</b><br /> <br /> In the pre-modern era, the God-Machine would still be somewhat ahead from the generally available technology of that time, but in my opionon not by a great margin. In my canon the God-Machine coevolved with human technology, spurring humans to create better technologies so it could enhance itself. So during the 13th century its most important infrastructure would mostly consist out of literal gears turning beneath the ground. In places where it currently uses modern technology it would in the past have used less efficient older technologies or the occult. The God Machine also wouldn't have been as widespread as it is now, as there is less mortal infrastructure to piggyback.<br /> <br /> Its angels would probably be far more rudimentary during that time, and be created from more occult components instead of mechanical components. I'm against introducing very anachronistic technologies through the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T07:02:26-08:00","id":68402,"title":"","content":"This is why I'm hoping that the Dark Era for Demon will be a long way back, like Byzantium. In the meantime, I'd suggest huge rope-and-pulley systems that seem to be more robust and efficient than they should, water clocks (filled with strange alchemical substances that smell suspiciously like blood even if they don't look like it) (and heated with large lenses), and lot of carefully proportioned architecture. And a lot of mathematical imagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T08:04:11-08:00","id":68433,"title":"","content":"I can't remember whose idea it was, but I'm fond of the notion that older angels tend toward forms that resemble statuary when they aren't made of &quot;live flesh.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T07:50:59-08:00","id":71974,"title":"","content":"Another thing... Technology can be lost - or mostly lost, or temporarily lost - from the human world, but may not be lost by the God-Machine. For instance, the Antikythera Mechanism implies a knowledge of clockwork all the way back in 100BC, though it was worked by a hand crank rather than a spring - thus it's feasible for the God-Machine to have had clockwork in its infrastructure ever since then - perhaps powered by a dedicated angel, modified human, or gravity and gears. It might have had steam for almost as long (although not in a steampunk sense - aeolipiles aren't good for that scale of engineering (though a powerful one might be able to drive the crank for a larger clockwork mechanism) - and they're perfect for when an occult matrix demands something be spinning in just the right place. Archimedes screws, Babylonian lenses, Baghdad batteries, Roman concrete - all of that could be available to the God Machine in the 13th Century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T08:02:26-08:00","id":71982,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that TGM might have the only universities in existence for all that time, or might simply be a better engineer itself, superior to those iffy flesh-bag things.<br /> Nothing says TGM has to be limited to what <b>we</b> have managed to do after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T11:31:49-08:00","id":72097,"title":"","content":"Let's also note that it's entirely possible the God-Machine had modern technology all throughout history. Its origins and history are quite unknown to everyone. While the &quot;slightly more advanced technology than the current time&quot; is something that I, personally, prefer, it is in no way a requirement.<br /> <br /> As for your idea about communion being infrastructure, that's freaking awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T13:09:16-08:00","id":72173,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is probably able to Time travel. I am sure it has modern Technology in the past. I am also sure, when a medieval priest behold a Creature made of chromed cogs, with burning lasereyes and wings made of Tesla coils with Lightnings fleshing all over, he would cal it a nAngel or a Daemon.<br /> <br /> But I still like the Idea of Antikythera-like bronze mechanisms, working in the most ancient parts of the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T21:15:24-08:00","id":72456,"title":"","content":"I also like antikythera-machine kind of thing, and probably the only reason is that it is aesthetically cooler for me.<br /> <br /> For exactly the same reason, if I run a Demon/GMC story in the 1800s, the GM / infrastructure / demonic things would probably look like steam engines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:54:09-08:00","id":72705,"title":"","content":"I think that giving a potentially canonical answer to how advanced the GM was in the past would, by extension, prove or disprove some of the various theories on the GM, and thus would have to be handled with care. for example, if OP decided that the &quot;slightly more advanced than current&quot; is the tech level, it doesn't fit with any GMC group that, in their world, has a GM that's the Singularity travelling backwards in time to conquer the universe retroactively. Similarly, if the devs said the opposite (that the GM has always been ultra advanced), it nullifies the possibility that it was once weaker and has grown mighty from its human flock. Personally, as the GM has seemingly old fashioned tech and occult infrastructure now, i'd assume it had advanced infrastructure now. God is eternal--IT does not change. what changes is what Infrastructure a given viewer can recognize or identify, and what infrastructure looks too alien to be called anything but celestial. Beauty and technology are in the eye of the beholder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}